# The build-context allowlist for webapp-deploy/portal.Dockerfile. BuildKit reads
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` before `<context>/.dockerignore`, so this file, and not the app image's
# Dockerfile.dockerignore, decides what the portal image can see. Everything is excluded first; the
# lines that follow name what comes back (the last matching line wins).
#
# Keep it in step with portalContextFiles() in webapp-deploy/k8s/local-lib.mjs, which builds the
# narrow snapshot the Kubernetes rehearsal uses; webapp-deploy/release-edge.test.mjs checks both.
*

# What `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --filter "@agentforge/portal..."` reads: the workspace
# manifests and the lockfile.
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!.npmrc
!patches
!apps/*/package.json
!packages/*/package.json

# What the portal runs, and the SQL it applies by path at boot (docs/internal/portal/migrations,
# the backend team's files; the rest of docs/ stays out).
!apps/portal
!docs/internal/portal/migrations

# The two operational scripts the stack runs INSIDE this image: the DSN wrapper (entrypoint of the
# portal and of portal-prepare) and the one-shot that migrates as the schema owner and sets the app
# login's password (the Kubernetes rehearsal's, unchanged). Baked in, so they always match the image's
# sha and the release bundle needs no extra file.
!webapp-deploy/portal-entry.sh
!webapp-deploy/k8s/base/scripts/prepare-db.mjs

# Never, even inside the folders above: dependencies, build output, and local state.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.enc
**/.master-key
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-*
**/*.log

# The Nix build (docs/internal/nix-migration.md). `*` already keeps it out; these lines keep it out if an allow
# line above is ever widened.
flake.nix
flake.lock
nix
